<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">O'Donnell dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Ó Domhnaill</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The O'Donnells, Ó Domhnaill, were a branch of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cenel-conaill">Cenél Conaill</a> who ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-donegal">Tír Chonaill</a> in north-western Ireland from the 13th century to 1607. Based at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/donegal-castle">Donegal Castle</a> from 1474, they kept a strong fleet and Scottish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mercenary">mercenaries</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-hugh-odonnell">Red Hugh O'Donnell</a> led them in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nine-years-war">Nine Years' War</a>, and Rory O'Donnell's departure in the Flight of the Earls ended their rule.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/odonnell-dynasty.jpg" alt="O'Donnell dynasty" width="320" height="385" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: MostEpic · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Arms_of_the_house_of_O%27Donnell_(16th_century).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
